{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Sarai the wife of Abram had not borne.</b> This verse comes to inform us that the covenant preceded the seed, so that one should not say there is no chronological order and the seed preceded the covenant; therefore it says: 'And Sarai the wife of Abram had not borne.' <b>And she had an Egyptian maid servant.</b> She was a shifḥah melog, and he was obligated to provide her food, and he was not permitted to sell her." "<b>And her name was Hagar.</b> When Pharaoh gave his daughter to Sarah, he said to her: 'My daughter, may you be my leg-pulling (agrikh)'; therefore she is called Hagar."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {1 "The reading 'agrikh' follows a folk etymology for הגר from לגור, 'to drag/pull'; the word is unusual and possibly corrupt in the witnesses."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:04:24.826831118Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}